      "layer": "governance_institutional",
      "tag": "internal_fragmentation",
      "direction": "decline",
      "description": "Urban cantons (Zurich, Bern) and rural cantons (Uri, Schwyz) had irreconcilable political cultures. The Old Zurich War (1440–46) nearly dissolved the confederation; only shared military interests prevented permanent fragmentation.",
